The value of $y$ that is not attainable is the value of $y$ that makes the denominator of the fraction $2x+3$ equal to $0$. Therefore, we set $2x+3=0$ and solve for $x$ to find $x=-\frac{3}{2}$.

Next, we substitute $x=-\frac{3}{2}$ into the numerator of the fraction $1-x$ to find the value of $y$ that is not attainable.
\begin{align*}
y &= \frac{1-\left(-\frac{3}{2}\right)}{2\left(-\frac{3}{2}\right)+3} \\
&= \frac{1+\frac{3}{2}}{-3+3} \\
&= \frac{\frac{5}{2}}{0} \\
&= \boxed{\text{undefined}}
\end{align*}
The value of $y$ that is not attainable is undefined.
